  - "Common root cause: price-only technical indicators show no directional edge on liquid BTC/ETH 1h. KB finding (ema_spread_trend_continuation_v1_auto) documents pattern: 'EMA crossover is a textbook, universally-taught technical signal on the most liquid crypto pair — consistent with no price-only technical indicator (RSI, Keltner in any variant, now EMA spread) showing exploitable directional content on BTC/ETH 1h.'"
  - "Structural barrier: ER-detector is Pareto-blocked on 1h BTC/ETH (cannot achieve [10-40% activation] AND [≤4 transitions/window] simultaneously); regime-conditional findings suffer small-sample bias."

recommendation: continue

recommendation_rationale: >
  CORRECTED 2026-07-09 (the premise below was stale -- see history note at end).
  The campaign exhausted price-only technical signals (RSI, Keltner variants, EMA,
  MACD) on BTC/ETH 1h with consistent root cause (signal_quality / already_priced_in).
  Run_054 escalated to daily-timeframe SMA(100) trend-following -- a genuinely
  distinct search space from the 1h oscillators/channels already exhausted.
  Run_054 IS NOW COMPLETE under the fixed code (bar-level/trades-file trade-count
  audit closed clean, 117 trades, zero mismatches -- see
  campaign_knowledge_base.yaml's p4_sma_trend_longonly_daily_auto). Result:
  protocol_verdict=kill, status=pivot -- NOT "no edge". The signal has a real,
  positive per-trade edge (per_trade_expectancy_bps=1050.5, t=1.91) that is
  negated by whipsaw losses in choppy regimes under this ungated formulation;
  root_cause=signal_regime_mismatch_ungated. The explicit, live pivot thread is
  a regime-gated SMA(100)-daily variant (a NEW hypothesis registration, not a
  reactivation of the ungated finding). Whether this satisfies
  config/detector_wishlist.yaml's daily_timeframe_er_overlay A2.3 trigger
  (confirmed ungated edge + regime-dependent performance -- both arguably present
  here) is an operator decision per RUNBOOK.md, not resolved by this entry.
  Recommendation is to continue the campaign pending that operator call, rather
  than either building the regime-gated variant unilaterally or treating
  run_054 as fully closed-out with no further thread.

  SUPERSEDED PREMISE (2026-07-09, earlier same day): this rationale previously
  said "run_054 has not been re-run with fixed code" -- that was true when this
  review first ran, but the fix was completed and the corrected verdict derived
  from stored (uncontaminated) artifacts within the same day, without a full
  backtest re-run. Preserved here for the record, not as current guidance.

budget_assessment: "Runs used: 33 (exact campaign_budget unknown from campaign_state.yaml, but implied high given 8+ reframes and escalations across instruments/timeframes). Usage ratio likely <0.5 of typical campaign budgets. Run_054 (P4_ts_trend, daily SMA trend-following) is now complete: kill/pivot on the ungated formulation, with a specific regime-gating pivot thread identified (see recommendation_rationale and campaign_knowledge_base.yaml). Next highest-information step is the operator's detector_wishlist.yaml trigger determination, not a new backtest."

